      <technology>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Technology: An average chainsaw weights about 7 kg. It is assumed that about 5.4 kg are unalloyed steel. The remaining 1.6 kg consists of the chain (0.4 kg) and the running rail (blade). Chain and running rail are made of highly alloyed steel. Service life of a chainsaw is around 2"500 service hours. The chain is replaced every 65 service hours; the running rail is replaced every 200 hours.</text>
        </comment>
      </technology>
